=== WHAT MUST CHANGE FOR A PASS ===
1. (C5, defect) Normalise as_of to a consistent day boundary before
   FilterByDateRange so the truncation cannot include tomorrow's rows west of
   UTC, and so the handler's boundary agrees with BalanceAt's dayOf boundary.
   Add a test pinning the today/tomorrow edge that fails under at least one
   non-UTC TZ today.
2. (C4b, brief criterion 3) Either keep the default path's reference_amount
   identical to pre-R5 behaviour, or get the change sanctioned and pin the NEW
   value with a fixture that actually contains a future-dated inbound paired
   transfer. The current TestGetBalanceProjectionDefaultAsOfUnchanged fixture
   has no transfers and no 3+-occurrence merchant, so it pins nothing the
   change could move.
3. (C4a, out of R5 scope, for the lead) Raise a separate task for
   internal/services/accounts/projection.go: byDay is keyed by time.Time values
   whose Location pointer differs between the writer (:136, UTC) and the reader
   (:149-150, Local when asOf = time.Now()), so no recurring occurrence is ever
   applied on any time.Now()-driven projection.
